Certainly! Here are the last three lines of the poem "If" by Rudyard Kipling:

"If you can not be wise, be brave;
If you can not be good, be true;
If you can not be happy, be happy now;
If you can not be free, be just."

Certainly! Here are the last three lines of the poem "If" by Rudyard Kipling:

"If you can dream—and not make dreams your master;
If you can think—and not make thought your guide;
If you can meet with Triumph and do not mourn;
If you can learn, and forgive, and let it go;"

These lines continue the theme of resilience and the importance of learning from one's experiences.
